userStories.description:
**Goal** — Persist the message an outcome is delivered on and deterministically rebuild byte-bounded delivery text for new-turn assignment.

**Motivation** — After #295 an approved, rejected or expired action leaves a `system` note, but nothing hands that note to the agent.

**Approach** — **2aw-D1 delivery column.** `PendingAction` gains `deliveredMessageId String?`, `@@index([threadId, deliveredAt])` and `@@index([deliveredMessageId])` (`api-data.md`: every filtered field is indexed). Migration `apps/api/prisma/migrations/20261024090000_pending_action_delivery/migration.sql`. No relation to `ChatMessage`: the column is an id only, like `approvalId`.

**2aw-D2 delivery text.** A pure module `apps/api/src/fleet/assistant/actions/outcome-delivery.ts` exports:

```ts
export const DELIVERY_HEADER = 'Updates on actions you proposed:';
export const MAX_DELIVERED_NOTES = 20;
export const DELIVERABLE_STATUSES = ['EXECUTED', 'FAILED', 'REJECTED', 'EXPIRED'] as const;

/**
 * The text the agent receives: the header, one note per line block, a blank line, then the user's text.
 * Notes are taken in the given order while the whole text stays within `maxBytes` UTF-8 bytes; the first note
 * that does not fit stops the list. No note fits, or none given: the user's text unchanged, delivered 0.
 */
export function deliveryText(notes: readonly string[], userText: string, maxBytes: number): { text: string; delivered: number } {
  const fits = (text: string): boolean => Buffer.byteLength(text, 'utf8') <= maxBytes;
  let delivered = 0;
  let text = userText;
  for (const [i] of notes.entries()) {
    const candidate = `${DELIVERY_HEADER}\n${notes.slice(0, i + 1).join('\n')}\n\n${userText}`;
    if (!fits(candidate)) break;
    delivered = i + 1;
    text = candidate;
  }
  return { text, delivered };
}
```

The notes are `outcomeNote(action)` (`outcome-note.ts`), rebuilt from the action, never read back from the `system` messages. `maxBytes` is `THREAD_LIMITS.messageMaxBytes` (32,768, `apps/api/src/fleet/common/thread-jobs.ts:24`), the bound the runner enforces on both `THREAD_INPUT` text and `initialMessage.text`.

**2aw-D4 new-turn assign.** `PrismaFleetJobRepository.findThreadAssign` builds `initialMessage.text` as `deliveryText(notes, message.content, THREAD_LIMITS.messageMaxBytes).text`, where `notes` are the `outcomeNote`s of the actions whose `deliveredMessageId` is the initial message's id, ordered by `createdAt` then `id`. It writes nothing, so every assign of the same job answers the same text. When the turn has no `initialMessageId`, it reads no actions at all and `initialMessage` stays null.

**`PendingActionRecord`** (`pending-action.domain.ts`). Target: gains the optional `deliveredMessageId?: string | null` (optional, so the existing spec literals without it still type-check), mapped by `prisma-pending-action.repository.ts`.

Implementation and regression anchors: modify only PendingAction in schema.prisma; update the repository's create/update/read mappings. Add AC-10 to prisma-fleet-job.repository.find-thread-assign.spec.ts while preserving its existing no-delegate stubs and kind/title expectations. Create the pure-helper unit spec and PG integration spec listed in expectedFiles. Use assistant-actions-decide.integration.spec.ts seeding conventions. Apply the migration and regenerate the generated Prisma client; no generated source edits.

**Scope** — In: 2aw-D1, 2aw-D2, 2aw-D4, record mapping and deterministic assignment tests. Out: selecting or marking newly delivered actions in sendMessage (US-002); all web approvals, cards, notes and list race changes (US-003..US-007). Changes to the runner, the fleet protocol or `FLEET_PROTOCOL_VERSION`; the delivery text rides the existing `THREAD_INPUT` text and `initialMessage.text` fields. Translating outcome note texts or the delivery header; they stay English (2a-D9).

**Interface** — `export function deliveryText(notes: readonly string[], userText: string, maxBytes: number): { text: string; delivered: number }`; `deliveredMessageId?: string | null`; existing `findThreadAssign(jobId: string): Promise<ThreadAssign | null>` keeps its signature.
